From 7eb04b074fb4e73c9c7722ae3026d2323750d889 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rebelancap <7285817+rebelancap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:14:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openxr: Vivecraft OpenXR work (openxr@13eafae1) ported onto
 Multiloader-26.3

This is upstream code by the Vivecraft authors (LGPLv3), not ours. Upstream's
`openxr` branch (https://github.com/Vivecraft/VivecraftMod, 13eafae1 "update to
26.2 add vulkan support split rendering and swapchain ...") has not been updated
to Minecraft 26.3. This single squashed commit is the result of
`git merge 13eafae1` into Multiloader-26.3 @ 15a9011f ("bump to 1.3.18"), i.e.
everything openxr adds on top of its last Multiloader merge (dee18e33), with the
conflicts resolved and the openxr-only code adapted to the 26.3 APIs.

Adaptations made while merging (no new features):
- com.mojang.blaze3d.{opengl,vulkan,systems,textures,...} -> com.mojang.renderpearl.*
  in all openxr-only code, mixin targets and the access widener (class map
  taken from the 26.2 and 26.3 client jars).
- RenderSystem.getDevice().backend -> FrontendGpuDevice.backend in the moved
  graphics/opengl/OpenGLHelper and graphics/vulkan/VulkanHelper (26.3's change
  to the old helpers, which openxr had moved).
- VulkanCommandEncoder.textureInitCommandBuffer() -> objectInitCommandBuffer()
  (renamed in 26.3), access widener updated.
- RenderPass.bindTexture(name, view, sampler) -> setUniform(name, view, sampler).
- VulkanBackendVRMixin: 26.3's findPhysicalDevice calls
  checkDeviceSuitability(device, required, optional) (null = suitable) instead
  of isDeviceSuitable(device); the VR-GPU preference wraps that call now.
- DeviceCompat desktop OpenGL binding: 26.3 replaced GLFW with SDL3, so the
  Win32 HWND / X11 display come from SDL window properties and the WGL/GLX
  context and drawable from the current context.
- GLFW_MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT -> SDLMouse.SDL_BUTTON_LEFT in the input code openxr
  moved from MCOpenVR into MCVR; debug-modifier press/unpress from 26.3 kept in
  the moved InputAction.
- lwjgl_openxr_version 3.4.1 -> 3.4.3, matching the LWJGL that Minecraft 26.3
  ships (openxr pinned it to 26.2's 3.4.1).
